  "EditorMetadata": {
    "Description": "CE-397 - the FIRST AiPrimitive in the corpus hosted as an HsmGuard. Measured 2026-09-27 across every tracked .bp.json: 34 BTreeAction, 9 BTreeCondition, 2 HsmAction and ZERO HsmGuard, so the HSM GUARD hosting path had no asset at all and acceptance rail 4 of DESIGN_Hsm_Blueprint_Behaviour_Authoring.md could not be closed by existing content. Graph: EventEntry -\u003E Return, with GetParameter(Open) wired into Return\u0027s Success data-in pin (BP-131: an AiPrimitive\u0027s Return carries a runtime Success pin, so the verdict is decided by the seeded parameter rather than picked at author time). It is deliberately the smallest graph that is still a REAL guard - what is under test is the ID AGREEMENT between the blob a hosting HSM compiles and the thunk this asset\u0027s registrar registers, not the graph body. LINK ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: the Return node authors Pins:[] so Stage0_Rehydrate binds its incoming links POSITIONALLY against the pin order [In(exec), Success(data)] - the exec link must therefore be listed first. HsmPolledGuardDemo.hsm.json is the machine that binds this guard.",
